# Executive Summary

Terraform requires a backend to store its infrastructure state before it can provision Azure resources.

Because the backend itself cannot be created using the Terraform configuration that depends on it, this project adopts a dedicated bootstrap phase.

The bootstrap infrastructure is created once and remains independent from the platform deployment lifecycle.

---

# Architecture Overview

```text
                    Bootstrap Phase
                           │
                           ▼
            Azure Resource Group
                           │
                           ▼
            Azure Storage Account
                           │
                           ▼
               Blob Container (tfstate)
                           │
                           ▼
                 Terraform Remote State
                           │
                           ▼
          Azure Enterprise Cloud Foundation
```

The backend infrastructure is provisioned before the first Terraform deployment and becomes the persistent storage location for the platform state.

---

# Design Decisions

| **Decision** | **Rationale** |
|--------------|---------------|
| Dedicated bootstrap phase | Avoids circular dependency during initial deployment |
| Azure Storage Account | Native Terraform backend for Azure |
| Single backend infrastructure | Sufficient for the current project scope |
| Backend managed separately | Platform deployment remains independent from backend lifecycle |
| Manual bootstrap | Simple, transparent and appropriate for a reference architecture |

